-- dispatch: a constraint that a REBUILT set superseded answers its sites
-- ONCE (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §6.2 Rule U1, §6.3, A.57,
-- A.75).
--
-- A constraint set is a RANGE of an append-only table and is never edited
-- (§6.1 invariant 2), so joining two sets, or two constraints of one name,
-- copies the inputs to fresh indices and leaves the old ones behind. The
-- obligations already registered still name the old indices and
-- `resolved_methods` is keyed on the index, so before A.75 the input and
-- its replacement were two live obligations over one site list: each
-- called `emitSites` over the sites it held and wrote the same
-- `(inst, evidence_index)` twice, which is one argument passed twice at a
-- call whose slot count the emitter checks (`Lower.evidenceShapeOk`).
--
-- It takes two calls of a constrained function whose receiver variables
-- unify AFTER both were instantiated, which is what NESTING one inside the
-- other does:
--
--   - `nested` is the join of two constraints of ONE name. `put`'s `k` is
--     fresh at each call, and the inner call's result `Box k1` meets the
--     outer call's parameter `Box k2` only once both are in the table, so
--     Rule U1 joins `k1.compare` and `k2.compare` on the surviving root.
--     Both `site 46 0` and `site 48 0` were written twice.
--   - `annotated` is the control: the annotation pins `k` to `String`
--     before the nesting is checked, so each constraint is discharged and
--     marked before any join happens, and its two sites (59, 61) were
--     right all along.
--   - `twoNames` is the same defect through the OTHER half of a rebuild.
--     `put`'s `k.compare` and `tag`'s `k.eq` are different names on
--     different variables, so nothing is joined — the union simply COPIES
--     both onto a fresh range, and a copy strands its input exactly as a
--     join does. Both `site 70 0` and `site 72 0` were written twice.
pub type Box k
    = Box k


pub put : Box k, k → Box k
    where k.compare : k, k → Order
put box _ = box


pub tag : Box k, k → Box k
    where k.eq : k, k → Bool
tag box _ = box


pub size : Box k → Int
size _ = 1


pub nested : Int
nested = size (put (put (Box "z") "a") "b")


pub annotated : Box String
annotated = put (put (Box "z") "a") "b"


pub twoNames : Int
twoNames = size (tag (put (Box "z") "a") "b")
